  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 306 AM MDT Fri Jul 10 2026/ \n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nStrong upper level ridging is beginning to build into the region \nbringing hotter temperatures for most of the state this weekend \nparticularly Southwest, Central, and Eastern Montana. Dry, hot and \nbreezy conditions will start Friday afternoon through Monday as the \nupper level ridge amplifies over the Northern Plains and Central \nRockies. Areas for the highest gusts will be along the Northern \nRocky Mountain Front and in the valleys of Southwest Montana. \nSouthwesterly flow will give some slight chances for isolated \nshowers and thunderstorms over Western and Central Montana Friday \nafternoon as mid-level moisture and steep lapse rates will allow for \nterrain enhanced convection. Weekend high temperatures will be in \nthe upper 90s to low 100s across much of the state with a chance for \na 2-3 degree cooling effect on Sunday as upper level cirrus clouds \nmove over early afternoon. Nighttime lows will only be in the 60s \nfor many areas this weekend as as warm as around 70 in the\nMissouri breaks preventing meaningful overnight recovery. \nSouthwest MT and most higher elevations areas will see cooler lows\nin the upper 50s which will give some recovery. \n\nAs the ridge starts to broaden over CONUS next week, some embedded \ntroughs along with more moisture will influence the region beginning \nTuesday afternoon allowing for higher chances of daily showers and \nthunderstorms across Western and Central Montana, however \nseverity and exact timing is not known yet. - Akins\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nBelow are the probabilities for maximum temperatures reaching or\nexceeding 100F this weekend:\n             \n               Sat 7/11  Sun 7/12\nGreat Falls        30%       40%\nBozeman            10%       70%      \nHelena             30%       40%\nHavre              70%       70%\nCut Bank            0%        0%\nLewistown          10%       70%\nDillon              0%       20%\n\nHeat advisories remain in effect for Saturday through Monday to \nhighlight moderate to major heat risk with temperatures likely to \npeak Sunday but impacts continuing through Monday after repetitive\nhot days. The combination of hot and dry conditions with breezy \nafternoon winds will bring elevated fire weather concerns, \nparticularly across southwest MT where deepest daytime mixing will \nsupport wind gusts to around 30 mph both Saturday and Sunday \nafternoon. These conditions will accelerate the seasonal \ncuring/drying of vegetation. Hoenisch",
